# ── Production (Vercel, etc.) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required on Vercel: set in Project → Settings → Environment Variables for Production (and Preview if needed).
# Value = public HTTPS origin of your tg_bot API + /api/webapp (no trailing slash).
# Example: https://api.yourdomain.com/api/webapp
# Your tg_bot FastAPI must be reachable from the internet with HTTPS (Telegram opens the mini app over HTTPS).
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-api-host.example.com/api/webapp
#
# After deploy: set the bot’s MINI_APP_URL (tg_bot .env) to your Vercel URL, e.g. https://your-app.vercel.app

# ── Local dev ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave VITE_API_URL unset: the app calls /api/webapp and Vite proxies to FastAPI.
# VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Auto 2FA: must match the account’s Telegram cloud password (and ideally server twofa_password).
# WARNING: Vite inlines this into the JS bundle — anyone can read it. Use only if you accept that risk.
# VITE_CLOUD_PASSWORD=
